  "result": "I've written the plan, but I couldn't call ExitPlanMode because it isn't available in this session, so nothing has been changed yet.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts an option's names with `reverse=True`. Long names (`--verbose`) therefore come before short ones (`-v`), instead of the usual `-v, --verbose`.\n\n**Fix:** remove `reverse=True` from that `rv.sort(...)` call. The sort is stable, so names with the same prefix length keep their declaration order.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Run `tests/test_formatting.py`, `tests/test_options.py` and `tests/test_basic.py`. Some expected-output strings may encode the old order.\n- Check that `--help` for a command with `@click.option(\"--verbose\", \"-v\")` shows `-v, --verbose`.\n\nThe full plan is at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-sparkling-storm.md`. Tell me to proceed and I'll make the edit.",
